[context: test, namespace: shop]
checkout-7d9f8c6b5-x2k4q (shop) is CrashLoopBackOff: container "app" was OOMKilled: it exceeded its 128Mi memory limit.

FINDINGS
1. [critical/high] pod.oom.container: container "app" was OOMKilled: it exceeded its 128Mi memory limit
   why: The kernel OOM killer stopped the container because it used more memory than allowed (exit 137, reason OOMKilled). It will keep crashing until memory use and the limit agree.
   evidence (status): <<untrusted source="status">> lastState.terminated reason=OOMKilled exitCode=137 (4m ago) <</untrusted>>
   evidence (status): <<untrusted source="status">> restartCount=9 <</untrusted>>
   evidence (spec): resources.limits.memory=128Mi
   evidence (spec): heap flag -Xmx256m in env JAVA_OPTS exceeds the 128Mi limit
   fix: Set the heap well below the limit (for JVMs prefer -XX:MaxRAMPercentage=75 instead of -Xmx256m), or raise resources.limits.memory to at least 384Mi.
   docs: https://kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/configure-pod-container/assign-memory-resource/

